[deps
  [doc [#
The repositories `cx` builds on, each at a sha (RULED: RS-7).

THE FORMAT is spec/03-approved/process/repository-dependency-pins.md. One [dep]
row per pinned REPOSITORY -- not per module. `sha` is the pin; `tag` records
the release it was taken from; `v-fork` is carried by a V repository's row.
`cx deps sync` (the verb that carries scripts/deps_sync.cx, RULED: DEPSV-1;
`make deps-sync` calls it) reads this document, fetches each pin shallowly into
an ignored deps/<repo>/, and FAILS on a stale pin or a drifted checkout. It
never warns (#1591; #1589 "Risks": the previous stale-copy arrangement rotted
within weeks because nothing failed when it did).

THE FIRST ROW IS HERE (RULED: RS-12, #1591 item 11). `cx-platform-sso` is the
first extraction -- quietest first -- and this row is what makes `cx` a
consumer of it rather than its owner. The pinned checkout is a BUILD INPUT:
registry/modules.cxd's sso row names its spec, corpus and bundled source under
deps/cx-platform-sso/, vcx/code/stdlib_bundle.v embeds that source into the
four profile builds, and `make test-sso-interop` runs the step script out
of the same checkout. So `make deps-sync` is not a convenience here -- a tree
without deps/ cannot build the profile that carries sso, and it says so by
name instead of dropping the module (Makefile, `deps-present`).

`cx` is a migration path, never a gate (RS-7): when any repository releases,
`cx` tries the newest mutually green set; green advances the pins, red leaves
them and the finding lands on the repository that moved. No merge anywhere
waits on `cx`. A release cut ships whatever is pinned.

NO `url=` ON THE ROW, and that is deliberate: §2.2's default is this
repository's own `origin` with the final path segment replaced by `repo`, which
is exactly where cx-platform-sso is. A `url=` here would be a second answer to
a question the default already answers correctly, and it would rot the day the
organisation moves.

NON-BUILD ROWS (cx-private#1858, owner ruling (c) then (a)). The last six rows
-- cx-registry, cx-decisions and the four bindings -- are no build input: no
module word of theirs reaches the bundle and none carries a v-fork. They are
pinned so `make deps-sync` fetches their deps.cxd and repos-allocation-gate's
[front-door pins] join reads it, as it reads every pinned repository's; each
row's module= is the repository's own name (spec §2: it provides no module
namespace to this consumer). None of the six pins the front door any more:
(c) moved the artifacts they pinned it for to their homes -- the ABI vectors
conformance/abi.cxd to cx-core-code beside libcx and the test that proves them,
the ledger indexer into cx-decisions -- so the composition allow-list is
unchanged.
#]]

